#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65$." :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n⟨5 + 4t, 3 - 2t,-4 - 3t⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n- 7(5 + 4t) + 5(3 - 2t) + (-4 - 3t) &= -65 \\\\\n- 35 - 28t + 15 - 10t - 4 - 3t &= -65 \\\\\n- 41t &= -41 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨5 + 4(1), 3 - 2(1),-4 - 3(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨9, 1,-7⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9, 1, -7)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 3y + 2z - 7 &= 0 \\\\\n4x - 3y + 2z &= 7 \\\\\n⟨x, y, z⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n⟨1 + 2t, 3 + t, 1⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n4(1 + 2t) - 3(3 + t) + 2 \\cdot 1 &= 7 \\\\\n4 + 8t - 9 - 3t + 2 &= 7 \\\\\n5t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨1 + 2(2), 3 + (2), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 5, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5, 5, 1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n${x = 3 - 4t; y =-1 + 2t; z = 2 + 3t$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 4y + 6z + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n3(3 - 4t) + 4(-1 + 2t) + 6(2 + 3t) + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n9 - 12t - 4 + 8t + 12 + 18t + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n14t &= -42 \\\\\nt &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{x = 3 - 4(-3) = 15; y =-1 + 2(-3) =-7; z = 2 + 3(-3) =-7\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69b22d8-5f30-5e05-81bb-243ed724e1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-4, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117553} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce1910-9bcc-5251-b118-6aa04aaeb35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117554} {:answer/id #uuid "06faf094-268f-5487-9e0a-8dda830b16c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8, 1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117555} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea6e821-2c68-5890-9921-7e7988992607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117556} {:answer/id #uuid "79a2209b-6180-5a7d-9efd-5b7a99c8eed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7, 1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea6e821-2c68-5890-9921-7e7988992607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117556} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe66adf4-1b34-5a67-af27-8e9f1215ce5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117552}] :question/id #uuid "49e4fa98-401d-5c2d-a49c-1997a8550033" :question/math-academy-id "q-33203" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: r = ⟨ - 5, 0, 1⟩ + t⟨ - 3, 1, 0⟩, Π: - 3x + y - 2z + 27 = 0$."}]}
